========================================================================
SAFETY STATEMENT  (non-binding — a request, not a license term)
========================================================================
This statement is NOT part of the AGPL-3.0 grant and adds NO legal
conditions to it. (Adding binding restrictions on top of the AGPL would
actually violate the AGPL, so this is deliberately a promise we ask of
you, not a rule we impose on you.)

DriftCore was built so that the people a system serves stay in control
of it. If you build on this code, we ask — not require — that you carry
that intent forward:

  - Keep human oversight in place. Do not strip it out to make an
    autonomous system that no one can stop.
  - Do not repurpose this safety layer to defeat safety — for weapons
    targeting, for deceiving the people a system serves, or to remove a
    human's ability to halt the system.
  - Keep the audit trail honest. Tamper-evidence is the point.
  - If you improve the safety guarantees, share them back.

Capability without trustworthiness is the problem this project exists to
answer. If you fork it, please keep it open, and keep it safe.

For the future. For the kids.
